# stackcone Blog posts

When the user asks for a **blog post**, **guide**, or **how-to**, produce a published HTML article in `blog/posts/` and keep markdown source in `blog/md/`. Same visual system as `solutions/` (charts, Mermaid, tables, FAQ/HowTo JSON-LD). See `.cursor/rules/solution-posts.mdc` for shared HTML patterns (diagrams, pipeline, impl phases, chart.js).

## Source vs published (required)

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `blog/md/{slug}.md` | Authoring source — **not** a public URL |
| `blog/posts/{slug}/index.html` | Published page — canonical, sitemap, internal links |

- **Never** place `.md` files in `blog/posts/`.
- **Never** link to `.md` from HTML, `posts.json`, sitemap, or nav.
- `robots.txt` disallows `/blog/md/` — do not override with indexable links.
- Markdown sources and `_dev/` scripts are **removed before GitHub Pages deploy** (see `.github/scripts/prepare-pages.sh`); only `.html` is public.

## Deliverables (always)

1. `blog/md/{slug}.md` — markdown source (mirror of content)
2. `blog/posts/{slug}/index.html` — published page
3. Update `blog/posts.json` — add entry with `"author": "Amar Kumar"`
4. Update `sitemap.xml` — add `<url>` for the HTML page only
5. Code blocks use Monaco via `.learn-code-wrap` + `data-lang` (same as Learn). Include `/assets/monaco-code.css` and `/assets/monaco-code.js`.

**Slug:** lowercase, hyphenated (e.g. `how-sse-streaming-works-chatbots-llm-tokens`).

## posts.json entry

```json
{
  "id": "{slug}",
  "title": "Short outcome-focused title (no parenthetical subtitles)",
  "description": "Value + keywords in one sentence (under ~155 chars)",
  "href": "./posts/{slug}/",
  "date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "dateLabel": "Month YYYY",
  "author": "Amar Kumar",
  "category": "RAG | Data | API | Docs | Freelancing | Platform",
  "tags": ["3–6 tags"]
}
```

## Article structure

- Opening hook — problem or misconception, then what the reader will learn
- Table of contents with anchor links — single `<nav class="toc">` wrapping one `<ol>`; **no manual numbers inside `<li>`** (browser list styling adds them; duplicating causes `1. 1.` artifacts)
- H2 sections; code blocks and comparison tables where useful
- **Hero or section images** when they clarify the topic (see Images below)
- FAQ section + `FAQPage` JSON-LD when appropriate
- Related guides — link to other **`.html`** posts only
- CTA block at bottom — contact links **must** be root-absolute `href="/contact/"` (never `../../contact/`, which resolves to the broken `/blog/contact/` from `blog/posts/{slug}/`)

## Images (required when relevant)

**Do not generate images with AI.** Search the web for relevant official or freely usable assets, **download them into the repo**, and reference the local file from HTML.

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `blog/images/{slug}/` | Per-post image assets (PNG/SVG/WebP) |
| `blog/posts/{slug}/index.html` | Published page references `../../images/{slug}/…` |

### Workflow

1. Search for relevant images: official brand kits, Wikimedia Commons, vendor press kits, protocol logos, architecture diagrams from docs.
2. Save files under `blog/images/{slug}/` with descriptive names (e.g. `mcp-logo.png`, `openai.png`, `kimi-with-icon-light.png`).
3. Prefer **official colored brand assets** (press kits, Wikimedia Commons, vendor brand guides). Do **not** use monochrome/grey icon CDN packs (e.g. LobeHub `light/` PNGs) when a full-color logo exists.
4. Add images in the article with semantic HTML:

```html
<figure class="blog-figure">
  <img src="../images/{slug}/example.png" alt="Descriptive alt text" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy">
  <figcaption>Short caption with source credit when needed.</figcaption>
</figure>
```

5. For multi-logo comparisons, use `.model-logo-row` or `.agent-stack-row` (defined in `blog/blog.css`).
6. Set meaningful `alt` on every image. Use `loading="lazy"` for below-the-fold images.
7. Optionally set `og:image` / `twitter:image` and JSON-LD `image` to a local hero asset: `https://stackcone.com/blog/images/{slug}/hero.png`.
8. In `blog/md/{slug}.md`, mirror images as `![alt](../images/{slug}/file.png)` for authoring parity.

### Do not

- Hotlink external image URLs in published HTML (links break, bad for SEO).
- Generate synthetic hero art when a real logo, diagram, or screenshot exists.
- Omit `alt` text or use filename-only captions.

## SEO

Follow `.cursor/rules/seo-google.mdc`. Unique title, meta description, canonical (`https://stackcone.com/blog/posts/{slug}/`), OG/Twitter, `Article` + `BreadcrumbList` JSON-LD.

## Tone

- Practical how-to or explainer — not a sales pitch
- Write like a technical blog post, not SEO copy — **do not** open with "If you searched…", "Developers searching for…", or keyword-stuffed query lists; state the problem or misconception directly
- Past tense OK for real experience; avoid fake metrics
- Upwork/freelance topics: actionable advice, not job-board provenance labels

## Diagrams (flowcharts, architecture, decision trees)

Use **Mermaid** in published HTML — not ASCII box art in `<pre><code>`. See `.cursor/rules/solution-posts.mdc` for the `diagram-wrap` + `mermaid-pending` pattern, footer script order (`mermaid.min.js` → `../../../solutions/diagrams.js`), and node styling.

- **Flowcharts / decision trees / pipeline graphs** → Mermaid `flowchart TB` or `flowchart TD`
- **Directory trees / file listings** → plain `<pre><code>` (not Mermaid)
- Mirror Mermaid source in `blog/md/{slug}.md` as fenced ` ```mermaid ` blocks

## Syntax highlighting (required for code blocks)

Blog code uses **Monaco** — the same `.learn-code-wrap` + `data-lang` markup as Learn. Monaco tokenizes the language natively. **Do not** use highlight.js, Prism, static `kw`/`fn`/`str` spans, or `apply_highlights.py`.

### HTML shape

```html
<div class="learn-code-wrap" data-lang="python"><pre><code>from pathlib import Path

def chunk_text(text: str) -> list[dict]:
    return []</code></pre></div>
```

`data-lang` must be a Monaco language id: `python`, `javascript`, `typescript`, `java`, `dart`, `kotlin`, `ruby`, `go`, `sql`, `json`, `yaml`, `xml`, `html`, `shell`, `plaintext`. Escape `<` as `&lt;` and `&` as `&amp;` inside `<code>`.

### Page assets

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/monaco-code.css?v=16">
<script src="/assets/monaco-code.js?v=20" defer></script>
```

`script.js` also lazy-loads Monaco when it finds `pre > code`, but new posts should include the assets explicitly.

### Do not

- Hand-wrap tokens in `<span class="kw">` / `.fn` / `.str`
- Add highlight.js / Prism CDN
- Put a fenced block only in `.md` and expect it on the live page without updating `.html`
- Wrap Mermaid diagrams in `.learn-code-wrap`
